# Local development credentials for Feeder.
#
# Copy to `.env.local` (gitignored) and fill in your own values. Both are
# PUBLIC identifiers, not secrets: anything with a VITE_ prefix is inlined
# into the JavaScript bundle at build time and is readable by anyone who
# opens the deployed site. Never put a real secret behind a VITE_ prefix.
#
# In CI these come from repo Actions *variables* (not secrets) and are only
# wired into the production build job — see .github/workflows/deploy.yml.
#
# Where to get them: see README.md → "Self-hosting / forking".

# OAuth 2.0 Web client ID. Its authorized JavaScript origins must include
# http://localhost:5173 (the dev server port) and your deployed origin.
VITE_GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID=your-client-id.apps.googleusercontent.com

# Google Picker API key, restricted by HTTP referrer to those same origins and
# API-target-restricted to the Picker API. Used ONLY to initialise the Picker —
# never attached to a Sheets or Drive REST call, which authenticate with the
# user's OAuth bearer token alone.
VITE_GOOGLE_API_KEY=your-picker-api-key
